hifiberry-audiocontrol (0.8.8) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Move player definitions into /etc/audiocontrol/players.d/, one file per
    providing package. audiocontrol.json no longer ships a players array, and
    an existing one is migrated on upgrade.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 13:24:53 +0000

hifiberry-audiocontrol (0.8.7) trixie; urgency=medium

  * mpd: stop generating a cover art URL for radio streams. For a stream MPD
    reports the stream URL as the song's "file", so the generated
    /library/mpd/image/<base64> URL asked MPD for album art of a stream, which
    it can never provide ("Cannot get size for stream"). Every radio track was
    served a cover art URL that was guaranteed to 404, which sent the web UI
    into an endless retry loop on the Now Playing page.
  * mpd: use the station logo (coverart_url/logo_url from the cached URL
    metadata) as cover art when a song has none, so radio stations show their
    logo instead of a placeholder.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 09:40:00 +0000

hifiberry-audiocontrol (0.8.6) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Restart on player-include changes via a dpkg trigger on
    /etc/audiocontrol/players.d. merge_player_includes() reads that directory
    only at startup, so a player shipped by another package (hifiberry-usbaudio)
    stayed invisible until audiocontrol happened to be restarted.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Sat, 01 Aug 2026 10:00:00 +0000

